    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pairs\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI suggest this default configuration. I believe that is so much intuitive:\r\n \r\n ```lua\r\nmappings = {\r\n  -- Prevents the action if the cursor is just before any character or next to a \"\\\".\r\n  [\"(\"] = { action = \"open\", pair = \"()\", neigh_pattern = \"[^\\\\][%s%)%]%}]\" },\r\n  [\"[\"] = { action = \"open\", pair = \"[]\", neigh_pattern = \"[^\\\\][%s%)%]%}]\" },\r\n  [\"{\"] = { action = \"open\", pair = \"{}\", neigh_pattern = \"[^\\\\][%s%)%]%}]\" },\r\n  -- This is default (prevents the action if the cursor is just next to a \"\\\").\r\n  [\")\"] = { action = \"close\", pair = \"()\", neigh_pattern = \"[^\\\\].\" },\r\n  [\"]\"] = { action = \"close\", pair = \"[]\", neigh_pattern = \"[^\\\\].\" },\r\n  [\"}\"] = { action = \"close\", pair = \"{}\", neigh_pattern = \"[^\\\\].\" },\r\n  -- Prevents the action if the cursor is just before or next to any character.\r\n  ['\"'] = { action = \"closeopen\", pair = '\"\"', neigh_pattern = \"[^%w][^%w]\", register = { cr = false } },\r\n  [\"'\"] = { action = \"closeopen\", pair = \"''\", neigh_pattern = \"[^%w][^%w]\", register = { cr = false } },\r\n  [\"`\"] = { action = \"closeopen\", pair = \"``\", neigh_pattern = \"[^%w][^%w]\", register = { cr = false } },\r\n}\r\n-- 24-04-25\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, it is just a suggestion.\r\n\r\n## [Here is my config](https://github.com/Sarctiann/lazyvim_config/blob/main/lua/plugins/mini-pairs.lua)\r\n(I will update this setup to get the more intuitive behavior to me)",
